      "hints": [
        "Factorise $-1$ from the $x^2$ and $x$ terms.",
        "Complete the square on $x^2 + 6x$.",
        "Simplify into the form $a - (x + b)^2$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Rearrange and factorise the negative coefficient from the quadratic terms:\n$$1 - 6x - x^2 = -(x^2 + 6x) + 1$$",
        "Complete the square inside the bracket:\n$$x^2 + 6x = (x + 3)^2 - 3^2 = (x + 3)^2 - 9$$",
        "Substitute back and simplify:\n$$1 - 6x - x^2 = -[(x + 3)^2 - 9] + 1 = -(x + 3)^2 + 9 + 1 = 10 - (x + 3)^2$$"
      ],
